      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nOpened from the green WhatsApp mark in the sidebar strip, which is shown active. Before the page is ready the pane reads 'Opening WhatsApp…'.\n⟳ is 'Reload WhatsApp' (enabled once ready, also on F5), 🌐 is 'Open in your browser', and ⧉ moves the page with its browser into a window of its own.\nOne WebView2 serves every visit and is hidden, not closed, when you leave. Its profile stays on disk, so the QR code is scanned once. The server's /whatsapp API is not used.\nWhatsApp is the only web app (WEB_APP_WHATSAPP) the screen defines.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "originalText": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nOpened from the green WhatsApp mark in the sidebar strip, which is shown active. Before the page is ready the pane reads 'Opening WhatsApp…'.\n⟳ is 'Reload WhatsApp' (enabled once ready, also on F5), 🌐 is 'Open in your browser', and ⧉ moves the page with its browser into a window of its own.\nOne WebView2 serves every visit and is hidden, not closed, when you leave. Its profile stays on disk, so the QR code is scanned once. The server's /whatsapp API is not used.\nWhatsApp is the only web app (WEB_APP_WHATSAPP) the screen defines.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
